            <ArticleTitle>How Could I Balance Continuing to Work While Pursuing a Degree?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1188/17.CJON.127</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In October 2010, the Institute of Medicine released the report The Future of Nursing: Leading Change, Advancing Health, which called for 80% of all nurses to have a BSN degree by 2020. This expectation was overwhelming and, in the beginning, I felt like it was an insult. I have had my associate degree in nursing for more than 20 years. All I could ask was: How can I have worked so many years and now be considered a subpar nurse? Regardless, the fact remained that I needed to return to college and obtain a higher degree.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
